        "url": "https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/biography/stephen-miller",
        "title": "Stephen Miller — EBSCO Research Starters",
        "published_at": null,
        "checked_at": "2026-11-09",
        "excerpt": "Stephen Miller was born on August 23, 1985 ... After his 2003 high school graduation, Miller studied political science at Duke University ... Following his 2007 graduation from Duke, Miller worked as a press secretary for Michele Bachmann ... He then worked as the communications director for John Shadegg ... before working as a policy adviser for Alabama senator Jeff Sessions ... Miller soon was promoted to Sessions’s communications director. ... Miller joined Donald Trump’s presidential campaign in January 2016 as a senior policy adviser. ... Miller led a conservative nonprofit group, America First Legal Foundation. ... In 2025, Miller returned to the White House as deputy chief of staff for policy and homeland security adviser",
        "tier": 2
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "url": "https://www.britannica.com/biography/Stephen-Miller",
        "title": "Stephen Miller | Britannica",
        "published_at": null,
        "checked_at": "2026-11-09",
        "excerpt": "Miller later attended Duke University, where he studied political science ... He graduated from Duke in 2007. ... He was hired as a press secretary for U.S. Rep. Michele Bachmann (Minnesota) and later served as communications director for Rep. John Shadegg (Arizona). In 2009 Miller began working for Sen. Jeff Sessions (Alabama) ... Miller, who eventually became chief of communications ... He subsequently founded (2021) the America First Legal Foundation. ... Miller assumed the posts on January 20, 2025.",
        "tier": 2
      },
